From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 23:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP: extend SA Query cleanup to legacy MLD reconnects

The upstream SA Query timeout cleanup handles a station that still has an
MLD profile. A former MLD station may instead reconnect as a legacy STA on
an affiliated AP; its MLD profile has already been cleared by authentication,
but the earlier partner link entries still need to be removed. Cover this
case on an AP MLD while retaining the upstream full-client-state and
Open/SAE restrictions so FT and FILS keys remain intact.

Pass check_authorized=0 to ap_sta_re_add() because the timed-out SA Query
permits replacing the old association. Clear the timeout after rebuilding
the STA so the same association cannot trigger cleanup twice.

Patch-dependency: 990-02-AP-fix-legacy-station-roaming-between-MLD-links.patch

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -7619,15 +7619,16 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 	 * association. FT and FILS keep keys in the state machine.
 	 */
 	if (hapd->conf->wpa && (sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) &&
-	    sta->sa_query_timed_out && ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) &&
+	    sta->sa_query_timed_out && hapd->conf->mld_ap &&
 	    FULL_AP_CLIENT_STATE_SUPP(hapd->iface->drv_flags) &&
 	    (sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_OPEN ||
 	     sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_SAE)) {
 		ap_sta_free_wpa_sm(hapd, sta);
-		if (ap_sta_re_add(hapd, sta) < 0) {
+		if (ap_sta_re_add(hapd, sta, 0) < 0) {
 			resp = WLAN_STATUS_AP_UNABLE_TO_HANDLE_NEW_STA;
 			goto fail;
 		}
 		sta->flags |= WLAN_STA_AUTH;
+		ap_sta_set_sa_query_timeout(hapd, sta, 0);
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
